PART 7 — REAL NCTB TEXTBOOK LIBRARY

Academic content must be real.

This application must not contain fabricated textbooks, imaginary chapters or fictitious official materials.

7.1 Official sources

Use the National Curriculum and Textbook Board of Bangladesh as the primary textbook authority.

Official starting points:

- NCTB official website: https://nctb.gov.bd/
- Official 2026 textbook catalogue: https://nctb.gov.bd/pages/static-pages/695b98afc4774958d7b7044c
- Class 6 catalogue: https://nctb.gov.bd/pages/static-pages/695b987ac4774958d7b7040b
- Class 8 catalogue: https://nctb.gov.bd/pages/static-pages/695b9858c4774958d7b703d8
- Classes 9–10 catalogue: https://nctb.gov.bd/pages/static-pages/695b99afc4774958d7b70612

The importer must check the official source at the time of actual content ingestion.

Never assume that the most recent academic year is automatically the most recent downloadable PDF.

7.2 Academic-year correctness

At the planning date of 17 November 2026, the publicly indexed NCTB catalogue located for the secondary textbooks is the 2026 catalogue.

NCTB's 2027 textbook printing and updates are underway.

Therefore:

- Look for officially published 2027 digital editions when ingestion begins.
- If the official 2027 edition is genuinely available, verify and import it.
- If it is not available, use the most recent actually published and verified edition.
- Clearly show its actual academic year.
- Never relabel an older book as a newer edition.
- Never fabricate missing editions.
- Never treat printing tenders as proof that the finished textbook PDF has been released.

Support automatic textbook-version updates through the administrative content system.

7.3 Complete textbook ingestion

Implement a complete book-ingestion workflow.

For each real textbook:

- Obtain its official source.
- Record its original title.
- Record class.
- Record subject.
- Record medium.
- Record academic year.
- Record edition or version.
- Record official source.
- Record publication details where available.
- Record rights and permission status.
- Retrieve the original complete PDF where authorized.
- Extract actual page content where permitted.
- Preserve the original page sequence.
- Preserve meaningful formatting.
- Preserve diagrams and tables.
- Preserve Bangla text correctly.
- Preserve mathematical notation.
- Preserve page numbers.
- Record its content checksum.
- Validate total page count.
- Check that pages are not missing.
- Verify table-of-contents consistency.
- Allow editorial review before publication.

Do not create chapter structures by guessing.

Use the real textbook's own chapter order.

7.4 Copyright and distribution

An officially downloadable textbook is not automatically a blanket permission to rehost, redistribute or transform its complete contents commercially.

Verify the actual rights and usage terms before storing and republishing textbook content.

When redistribution permission is unclear:

- Keep the official source record.
- Provide a properly attributed link to the official material.
- Use approved viewing or embedding methods where available.
- Do not unlawfully mirror or redistribute the entire document.

Rights status must be stored in the content database.

A textbook cannot be published into the internal StudyQuest catalogue without an acceptable content-source and permission status.

